    "proof_limit": "One compiler profile; static MIR constant calls only. Indirect/dynamic calls, drop terminators requiring destructor analysis, and unrecognized local targets remain unknown. Compiler-generated nominal field layout edges without an explicit local Drop::drop implementation remain passive value-layout witnesses; only exact local Drop implementations create executable destructor-call edges. MIR is an unstable compiler output, pinned by compiler version and input hashes. DefIds extracted from MIR function-signature text are diagnostic hints only and may identify bound regions; local implementation joins require exact THIR FnDef identities plus HIR owner spans or exact rustdoc symbols. External trait calls require exact THIR FnDef evidence, a concrete receiver without local/generic type components, and closed trait type arguments (lifetime-only arguments are inert); an external path root alone is insufficient. A closure-containing external call resolves only its callee; closure bodies are separate MIR items and remain subject to their own call analysis. Local closure DefIds require an exact HIR owner-span join. Same-source provenance is included only when a provenance receipt is supplied; external calls without mapped local caller spans are counted separately."
  },
